    "text": "• Oscar nominations will be announced at 8:30 a.m. Eastern on Thursday.\n• Viewers can watch live on Oscar.com, Oscars.org, the academy’s digital platforms, and ABC's “Good Morning America.”\n• “Sinners” and “One Battle After Another” are expected to receive multiple nominations.\n• “Mel Brooks: The 99 Year Old Man!” is a documentary about Mel Brooks, debuting Thursday on HBO and HBO Max.\n• The 42nd Sundance Film Festival begins this week in Park City, Utah, and will be the last in its current location.\n• The festival will honor Robert Redford and will relocate to Boulder, Colorado, next January.\n• The production team of the Met Opera's “Carmen” requested their names be removed due to restaging decisions.\n• The restaging involved changes to the set, including removing a Jaguar and adding a motorcycle.\n• Duckwrth's album “All American F—Boy” is nominated for a Grammy for best immersive audio album.\n• “Mercy,” starring Chris Pratt, is a film about a detective on trial with an AI judge, opening in theaters Friday.\n• Taylor Swift, Kenny Loggins, and members of Kiss are among the 2026 Songwriters Hall of Fame inductees.\n• The induction ceremony will be held June 11 at the Marriott Marquis Hotel in New York City.\n• Dior's menswear show in Paris featured a stripped-back set and neon-yellow wigs.\n• Valentino Garavani, the fashion designer, is being honored in Rome with a public viewing.\n• His funeral will be held on Friday in the Basilica di Santa Maria degli Angeli e dei Martiri.\n• Georges Borchardt, a literary agent, has died at 97.\n• He represented authors like Elie Wiesel, Samuel Beckett, Ian McEwan, and Tracy Kidder.",
